<section class="sec" id="review" aria-labelledby="t-review">
  <h2 id="t-review"><span class="n">5</span> Docs that keep up with every commit</h2>
  <p class="lede"><span class="nt">After each commit,</span> <code>dockeeper review</code> lists the claims the change touched, the new code that nothing documents yet and the decisions nobody wrote down. Your agent reads that list and updates the docs as it goes.</p>
  <aside class="mn"><b>It never blocks</b>A <code>post-commit</code> hook runs it after the commit is made. Ask your agent to “review the docs on every commit” and it installs the hook. With <code>--desde main</code> it reviews a whole branch.
    <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/revision.py#revisar -->
  </aside>
  <div class="wide">
    <p class="term-label">After a commit that changed one function and added another</p>
<figure class="termwin">
<figcaption class="termbar"><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>post-commit hook — dockeeper review</figcaption>
<pre class="term"><span class="pr">$</span> git commit -m "feat: refunds"
<span class="c">dockeeper review · changes since HEAD~1 (85753313b3) · 1 code file · 0 documents</span>
Claims this change touches (review the text):
<span class="ch">CHANGED</span>          <span class="ac">docs/payments.md:3</span>  <span class="c">→</span> <span class="ac">src/payments.py#validate_payment</span>
New or changed code with no claim (worth adding to the docs?):
  <span class="mv">new</span>       <span class="ac">src/payments.py#refund</span> (3 lines) <span class="c">· already about that file: docs/payments.md</span>
Decisions in these commits not documented yet (dockeeper why):
  <span class="c">6abae57d27 2026-10-14</span>  refunds reuse the payment validation
<span class="c">[main 6abae57] feat: refunds</span></pre>
</figure>
